(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Cancer-associated thromboembolism represents a major morbidity risk, yet optimal) Tj
T*
(anticoagulation duration in low-risk presentations remains uncertain. This protocol) Tj
T*
(describes a randomized comparison of prolonged versus standard-duration anticoagulation in) Tj
T*
(cancer patients with hemodynamically stable pulmonary embolism, stratified by functional) Tj
T*
(status. Eligible participants will be randomly assigned to receive either 18 months or 6) Tj
T*
(months of oral anticoagulant therapy. Study stratification will account for performance) Tj
T*
(status \(fully active vs. restricted activity\), as this parameter may modify the risk-) Tj
T*
(benefit profile of extended treatment. Primary outcome will be objectively documented) Tj
T*
(recurrent thrombosis. Secondary outcomes will include bleeding complications graded by) Tj
T*
(severity and major adverse events. Enrollment targets approximately 200 participants) Tj
T*
(across both strata. Baseline characteristics, concurrent cancer treatments, and adherence) Tj
T*
(will be evaluated as potential effect modifiers. Study assessments will occur at regular) Tj
T*
(intervals throughout treatment and at a final safety follow-up visit.) Tj
